from review import card,save,DATE
i='TCS-3685';_,c=card(i);refs=c['references'];refs[0]['locator']='Sections 2.1–2.3, raw truth-table input and De Morgan leaf count; Theorem 3.1, worst-case bound; Section 5, conjectured uniform average-case hardness.'
refs += [dict(id='preprint',title='Cubic Formula Size Lower Bounds Based on Compositions with Majority',authors='Anna Gál; Avishay Tal; Adrian Trejo Nuñez',year=2018,url='https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2018/160/',pdf_url='https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2018/160/download/',locator='Original September 2018 preprint; same raw truth-table definition and concluding average-case claim.')]
issue='With the displayed raw truth-table definition and a uniform distribution on all input bits, a one-leaf formula already has inverse-polynomial advantage. If z is any address with maximal probability p_z≥1/n, the formula outputting the input table bit f(z) agrees with M_n with probability 1/2+p_z/2≥1/2+1/(2n). On a different address the two independent fair table bits agree with probability 1/2. Thus the literal inverse-polynomial claim, and the stated 2^{-o(log² n)} strengthening, cannot hold for unrestricted De Morgan formulas in this model. A corrected intended target would need a different agreement regime, input distribution, encoding or other source-supported change; none is invented here.'
notes=['Recovered the raw truth-table majority-address function, all input bits in the uniform distribution and leaf-count formula model.','Restored the squared logarithm and almost-cubic target from the truncated sentence.','Found an elementary formulation inconsistency: one table-bit literal already has inverse-polynomial agreement advantage.','Separated this editorial sanity check from the paper’s valid worst-case composition theorem and from any proposed replacement problem.','Read the original preprint and conference version and searched later formula-composition work and corrections.']
save(i,dict(title='Average-case formula hardness of the majority Andreev function',formal='The source conjectures that achieving agreement 1/2+1/poly(n), or even 1/2+2^{-o((log n)²)}, with the majority-based Andreev function M_n under the uniform input distribution requires almost cubic De Morgan formula size. Recovering its displayed input model exposes a conflict: M_n receives the unencoded truth table of an arbitrary Boolean function as part of its input, and a single bit of that table already gives agreement at least 1/2+1/(2n). Consequently this extracted conjecture is not certified as an open lower-bound proposition; its intended distribution, input encoding or agreement requirement needs correction.',definitions='Use the source’s integral parameter convention: n=2ᵇ, b=log₂n and m=n/b are integers, with n tending to infinity along admissible sizes. The input comprises an n-bit string t, indexed by addresses z∈{0,1}ᵇ in lexicographic order, and b disjoint rows x₁,…,x_b of m bits each. Thus there are 2n independent input bits. Interpret t as the truth table of f_t:{0,1}ᵇ→{0,1}, f_t(z)=t_z. For a row x, Maj_m(x)=1 if its Hamming weight is at least ⌈m/2⌉ and zero otherwise; ties for even m output one. Put J(x)=(Maj_m(x₁),…,Maj_m(x_b)) and M_n(t,x)=t_{J(x)}. In the literal uniform reading, t is a string of independent fair bits, independent of all fair row bits; f_t is not fixed in advance or encoded by an error-correcting code. A De Morgan formula is a tree with binary AND/OR gates and negations, equivalently negations pushed to input literals. Its size is the number of leaf occurrences; gates are not allowed to share subcomputations, and all 2n input coordinates, including table bits, are available as literals. The formula is deterministic and may be chosen separately at each input length. Agreement is Pr_{(t,x) uniform}[F_n(t,x)=M_n(t,x)]. A table-bit literal has size one. In asymptotic notation, inverse-polynomial advantage includes 1/(2n), while 2^{-o((log₂n)²)} denotes an advantage whose negative logarithm grows more slowly than (log₂n)²; 1/(2n) is also in that regime. Almost cubic is the source’s informal near-n³ size requirement, which cannot be reconciled with the one-leaf observation under these conventions.',question_type='yes_no',answer_criterion='First recover a source-supported correction that yields a coherent average-case lower-bound proposition, with exact function, distribution, agreement threshold and size quantifiers. The literal broad advantage claims above fail the one-leaf check and cannot be accepted as an open benchmark. A worst-case size lower bound does not resolve the missing intended average-case formulation. Replacing the raw table by a coded function or fixing a particular outer function would change the target and requires provenance.',context_blocks=[dict(title='The input table is material',text='The source defines M_n on the raw truth table t and independent row inputs. Its worst-case proof may fix t to a hard outer function, but that does not make t fixed in the displayed uniform average-case question.',citation='primary'),dict(title='Editorial consistency check',text='Choose an address z maximizing Pr[J(x)=z], which is at least 1/n among n possibilities. The literal t_z is correct whenever J=z. Conditional on J≠z, the two selected truth-table bits are independent fair bits, so it is correct half the time. Its agreement is therefore 1/2+Pr[J=z]/2≥1/2+1/(2n). This is a direct check of the displayed definition, not a claim about a different coded or fixed-table function.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The worst-case theorem is a different statement',text='The paper establishes an almost cubic worst-case lower bound through composition with majority. That theorem concerns exact computation on every input; the one-leaf average-case observation does not contradict it.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The source versions do not resolve the ambiguity',text='The original ECCC preprint retains the raw-table definition and the same broad average-case claim. Searches did not locate a correction specifying a different model for this card.',citation='preprint')],why='The intended question would measure how robust a nearly cubic formula lower bound is under approximation, but the precise input representation is essential to any such hardness claim.',references=refs,progress=[dict(date='2018-09-12',text='The preprint establishes a worst-case composition result and proposes the average-case extension.',citation='preprint'),dict(date='2019',text='The conference version retains the raw-table definition and the concluding conjecture.',citation='primary'),dict(date=DATE,text='Editorial review finds that the literal uniform raw-table reading admits inverse-polynomial advantage from one input leaf; the intended corrected target remains unresolved.',citation='primary')],status='uncertain',status_note='Read the complete function definitions and concluding paragraph in the preprint and conference versions. The simple conditioning calculation in this review contradicts the literal inverse-polynomial and 2^{-o(log² n)} advantage claims. Subsequent searches through 12 September 2026 did not locate a source correction. This records a formulation problem, not a claim to resolve a different intended research question or an independent audit of the paper’s proofs.',model_self_contained=False,requires_context=True,statement_review=dict(status='needs_specification',reviewed_on=DATE,notes=notes,remaining_issue=issue),review_note=issue,importance=dict(score=c['importance']['score'],method='editorial',reason='Potentially significant average-case robustness of formula lower bounds, but the raw-table formulation has an explicit consistency defect. Existing score retained.',assessed_on=DATE),working_summary=dict(sentences=['The majority Andreev function uses row majorities as an address into an input truth table.','The source proposes almost cubic formula hardness even for inverse-polynomial agreement advantage under uniform input.','In that literal model, one table-bit literal already has agreement at least 1/2+1/(2n).','This does not contradict the source’s worst-case formula theorem, but it prevents certifying the extracted average-case claim.','The intended distribution, encoding or advantage threshold must be corrected from a source before the card becomes a complete open problem.'],basis='saved_sources',source_basis='source-text',written_on=DATE,source_refs=['primary','preprint'])),notes=notes,checked_sources=[r['url'] for r in refs]+['https://eccc.weizmann.ac.il/report/2020/180/'],state='improved_unfinished')
